<title>USA: TWA to lay off 268 workers -- paper.</title>
<headline>TWA to lay off 268 workers -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc plans to lay off about eight percent of the workforce at its overhaul base here, the Kansas City Star newspaper reported Sunday.</p>
<p>A TWA spokesman said the layoffs would be effective June 2 and would affect 268 mechanics and workers, the paper reported. The overhaul base employs about 3,100 people.</p>
<p>The layoffs would follow cuts made by TWA earlier this year at Kennedy International Airport in New York. The airline eliminated many flights and laid off about 700 employees.</p>
<p>((-- Kansas City bureau, 816 561-8671))</p>
